.Sh ENVIRONMENT
Options override the environment, which overrides the configuration file.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CREATURE_COMMUNICATOR_GATEWAY_CONFIG
Configuration file, when
.Fl -config
is not given.
.It Ev SERVER_HOSTNAME , Ev SERVER_PORT
HTTP bind address and port.
.It Ev CREATURE_WORLD_URL
Creature World API URL.
.It Ev OTEL_*
OpenTelemetry export (OTEL_SERVICE_NAME, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS,
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL).
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/creature/communicator-gateway.json
Configuration: bind address, port and the World URL. A conffile; upgrades keep local edits.
.It Pa /etc/default/creature-communicator-gateway
Environment for the service, mode 0600.
.It Pa /usr/lib/systemd/system/creature-communicator-gateway.service
The unit. It runs as a
.Li DynamicUser
and is not started on install:
.Dl systemctl enable --now creature-communicator-gateway
.It Pa /usr/share/doc/creature-communicator-gateway/creature-communicator-gateway-manual.md
The operator's manual, including every configuration key.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl creature-communicator-gateway --port 8002 --world-url http://127.0.0.1:8001/world/v1
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr creature-world 8
